WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:06.629
"According to our information, the enemy has
listed me as target number one, and my family

00:00:06.629 --> 00:00:08.890
as target number two.

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:17.520
They want to destroy the country politically,
terminating the head of state."

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:22.560
Desperate words from the Ukrainian president
on the day after Russia invaded his country.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:27.020
Desperate words from a man who, only a couple
of years ago, played the piano on TV with

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:34.600
his trousers around his ankles …and without
using his hands.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:38.230
Volodymyr Zelenskyy has undergone an extraordinary
transformation

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:40.850
…from an entertainer dancing in high heels

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:45.489
…to a wartime leader in green khaki t-shirts.

00:00:45.489 --> 00:00:49.760
Zelenskyy's regular selfie-style addresses
have won him the eyes and ears, as well as

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:52.489
the hearts, of many at home and abroad.

00:00:52.489 --> 00:00:58.059
He has also received standing ovations from
politicians around the world.

00:00:58.059 --> 00:01:02.500
Many say that much of his remarkable success
in leading his country against Russia’s

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.530
invasion stems from what he says and how he
says it.

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:08.619
But how exactly does Zelenskyy communicate?

00:01:08.619 --> 00:01:13.520
Let’s take a closer look.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:19.950
The skills that are required of playing a
president are kind of the skills required

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:22.229
for the public presentation of a presidency.

00:01:22.229 --> 00:01:26.250
It’s now a well-known fact that, before
becoming the president of Ukraine, Zelenskyy

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:28.150
spent a career in show business.

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:32.750
He won Ukraine’s version of ‘Dancing with
the Stars’ back in 2006

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:37.700
…and was the Ukrainian voice behind “Paddington
Bear”.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:42.119
Zelenskyy went on to star in the satirical
TV show ‘Servant of the People’

00:01:42.119 --> 00:01:49.930
where he played a high-school teacher who
is unexpectedly elected President of Ukraine.

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:55.850
I'm convinced that his experience as an actor
is definitely an asset for him.

00:01:55.850 --> 00:02:04.910
The ability to have presence, the ability
to remember lines, to read a speech without

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:10.969
it being clear that you are reading, all of
those things from Zelenskyy's prior background

00:02:10.969 --> 00:02:16.389
as an actor come into very good use as the
leader of Ukraine.

00:02:16.389 --> 00:02:20.749
… abilities that seem more relevant than
ever in the age of digital mass communication.

00:02:20.749 --> 00:02:22.329
That’s probably what you need.

00:02:22.329 --> 00:02:24.419
You need to be informal, you need to be memeworthy.

00:02:24.419 --> 00:02:27.230
“We are all here.

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:35.659
Our citizens are here, our soldiers are here
and we are here.”

00:02:35.659 --> 00:02:40.840
Defiant words from Zelenskyy, standing surrounded
by members of his cabinet, after rumors occurred

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:42.870
he had fled the country.

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:47.959
A 32-second selfie-style video, filmed in
the streets of Kyiv – and perfect for going

00:02:47.959 --> 00:02:48.959
viral.

00:02:48.959 --> 00:02:53.879
What he does with that video is he has all
the tropes that you need to be successful

00:02:53.879 --> 00:02:55.500
in the social media age.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:59.980
It's short, it's informal, it's colloquial.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:02.371
That's something that they've always been
effective at.

00:03:02.371 --> 00:03:07.260
That's why Zelenskyy is the president of Ukraine
– because they were effective in communicating

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:11.760
to young Ukrainians through precisely these
types of social media outlets.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:16.219
Zelenskyy led an unorthodox presidential campaign
in 2019,

00:03:16.219 --> 00:03:19.389
drawing on his fame as an actor.

00:03:19.389 --> 00:03:22.790
He gave few interviews and instead relied
on social media.

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:27.359
Literally, within a few months, they had set
up a campaign based around social media using

00:03:27.359 --> 00:03:29.220
Instagram instead of Twitter, for instance.

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:32.949
Twitter was something they thought was for
political nerds and journalists.

00:03:32.949 --> 00:03:37.290
Instagram was the media to reach ordinary
people who weren't very political and weren't

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:38.889
following the news in much detail.

00:03:38.889 --> 00:03:49.900
The strategy proved successful, resulting
in an unexpected landslide victory.

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:54.349
But he failed to deliver on one of his main
campaign promises – to end the conflict

00:03:54.349 --> 00:03:56.540
in eastern Ukraine.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.269
And then there were the Pandora Papers.

00:03:58.269 --> 00:04:03.379
The investigative report, conducted by an
international network of journalists, revealed

00:04:03.379 --> 00:04:05.959
that Zelenskyy had ties to offshore companies.

00:04:05.959 --> 00:04:11.680
That didn’t go down well with Ukrainians
given that he had vowed to end corruption.

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:15.879
His approval ratings were rock bottom before
Russia invaded.

00:04:15.879 --> 00:04:21.260
But since then, public support for Zelenskyy
has soared to over 90%.

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:27.030
Even people who were definitely his political
opponents before that are giving him recognition

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:31.210
for what he's achieved in terms of the communication
within the country, in terms of his decision

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:35.849
not to leave Kyiv when it seemed in those
early days that Russia would roll into Kyiv

00:04:35.849 --> 00:04:41.479
within a matter of days when he told the Americans
that he needed ammunition and not a ride.

00:04:41.479 --> 00:04:45.259
“‘To be or not to be.'

00:04:45.259 --> 00:04:48.240
You know this is a Shakespearian question.”

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:56.600
“Remember Pearl Harbor, that terrible morning
of December 7, 1941, when your sky was black

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:59.879
from the planes attacking you.”

00:04:59.879 --> 00:05:05.120
“Chancellor Scholz, tear down this wall.”

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:09.229
Since the start of the war, Zelenskyy has
been on a virtual world tour,

00:05:09.229 --> 00:05:12.710
making his plea for support in front of various
parliaments,

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:18.240
repeating the same message over and over again
– but each time customized for his audience.

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:25.320
When he is addressing a foreign parliament,
he has been primed on the sort of the key

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:31.229
elements of national history that he should
touch upon that will lead his listeners to

00:05:31.229 --> 00:05:35.439
identify with the Ukrainian cause in this
particular moment.

00:05:35.439 --> 00:05:39.379
And his listeners do seem to identify with
the Ukrainian cause…

00:05:39.379 --> 00:05:45.130
Germany for instance reversed decades of foreign
policy and agreed to send weapons to Ukraine.

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:49.699
However, one of Zelenskyy’s demands to foreign
leaders hasn’t been met – his call to

00:05:49.699 --> 00:05:52.719
establish a no-fly zone over Ukraine.

00:05:52.719 --> 00:05:57.729
Some say that, maybe, Zelenskyy is deliberately
asking for more than he expects to gain – a

00:05:57.729 --> 00:06:00.110
strategic communication maneuver.

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:09.669
I think he knows that if NATO was actually
fighting in Ukraine, it would start a third

00:06:09.669 --> 00:06:11.129
world war.

00:06:11.129 --> 00:06:18.780
But nevertheless, he asked, for example, for
no-fly zones in Ukraine to avoid Russian bombardments.

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:24.030
And in the US, Congress could not offer him
that.

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:28.749
But they decided to send more anti-aircraft
bombs.

00:06:28.749 --> 00:06:33.090
And apart from Ukrainians at home and leaders
abroad, Zelenskyy clearly has another target

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:35.560
audience in mind…

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:41.479
“I want to address today the people of Russia.

00:06:41.479 --> 00:06:48.389
I am addressing you not as a president, I
am addressing you as a citizen of Ukraine.”

00:06:48.389 --> 00:06:51.410
Zelenskyy speaking on the eve of the Russian
invasion,

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:55.669
setting himself apart from Russian President
Vladimir Putin.

00:06:55.669 --> 00:07:01.460
He's certainly the antithesis to Putin in
terms of his communication strategy.

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:09.830
So Putin has been giving hour-long lectures
about obscure aspects of Russian and Ukrainian

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:11.330
history.

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:19.469
[...] Zelenskyy has been able to do these
shorter attention-grabbing and spreadable

00:07:19.469 --> 00:07:23.229
ideas, much more so than Putin has.

00:07:23.229 --> 00:07:28.080
And it is not just his communication strategy
that makes Zelenskyy a counterpoint to Putin.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:31.729
The Russian president is known for projecting
a kind of hypermasculinity.

00:07:31.729 --> 00:07:38.240
The word macho is almost perfectly positioned
to describe Putin because he is very keen

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:45.430
to present himself as shirtless, on horseback
and as an excellent athlete, succeeding at

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:49.539
having power over other people through the
use of his body.

00:07:49.539 --> 00:07:53.360
Zelenskyy is not concerned with those things,
and it would be tempting to say that this

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:55.479
is post-masculinity.

00:07:55.479 --> 00:08:00.620
But in fact I think it's just a different
kind of way of being a man in the world, one

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:07.500
that is not quite so concerned about maintaining
its dignity and its status as man all the

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:08.610
time.

00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:16.590
Zelenskyy has been presenting himself as unshaven,
exhausted, vulnerable – but determined nonetheless.

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:21.490
We look at him and we see someone who is an
ordinary person who's been called upon to

00:08:21.490 --> 00:08:23.690
do something extraordinary.

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:26.550
And that, to many of us, feels heroic.

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:32.190
So he is, in an odd sense, heroic precisely
because he's not a natural born hero.

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:37.070
From entertainer to wartime leader – Volodymyr
Zelenskyy has been delivering a compelling

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:40.479
performance in a role he probably never wanted
to play.

